WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.843 --> 00:00:02.851
- [Voiceover] This is Ping,

00:00:02.851 --> 00:00:05.683
a southern three-banded armadillo.

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:07.644
Predators, look elsewhere.

00:00:07.644 --> 00:00:11.814
You'll have a hard time
cracking open this critter.

00:00:11.814 --> 00:00:15.193
Like all armadillos, they
are covered by bony plates

00:00:15.193 --> 00:00:16.946
that make up their shell.

00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:19.207
But the southern three-banded armadillo

00:00:19.207 --> 00:00:21.202
is the only armadillo species

00:00:21.202 --> 00:00:22.574
that can roll themselves

00:00:22.574 --> 00:00:25.954
into a near-perfect ball when threatened.

00:00:25.954 --> 00:00:27.622
These little guys are native

00:00:27.622 --> 00:00:29.379
to central South America

00:00:29.379 --> 00:00:31.626
and prefer dry vegetation.

00:00:31.626 --> 00:00:33.465
There, they feed off insects

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:36.380
that they dig up with their
sharp, powerful claws,

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:40.504
and gather with long,
sticky, straw-like tongue.

00:00:40.504 --> 00:00:43.512
But even body armor can't
protect this species

00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:46.850
from numerous human-made threats.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.058
On top of a dwindling habitat,

00:00:49.058 --> 00:00:53.100
they are hunted heavily
for food and the pet trade.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.767
This is the southern
three-banded armadillo.

